dialogue cohesion_barbarian_knight
title: First in
trigger: Cohesion barbarian knight level=2
once
speaker commander $commander
speaker barbarian barbarian
speaker knight knight

node open commander
  The Knight's shield lies face up by the fire with a fresh axe-bite in the rim. The Barbarian put it there, and the Knight has not stopped looking at it.
  -> bite

node bite knight
  You went through my line today. Straight through it. You're meant to be behind the shield, not on the other side of it swinging back.
  -> behind

node behind barbarian
  I've never been behind anyone. Not at home, not on the moors. First in. That's what I'm for.
  -> stand

node stand knight
  First in is what I'm for. Stand before the hold. It's cut in the rim, next to your axe mark. So which of us goes first, Commander? You decide, and we'll both hate it.
  * The Knight. The shield's made for it. The Barbarian goes second and hits harder for the wait. -> knight_first
    do: AddCohesion barbarian knight 6
    do: AddTrust barbarian -3
    do: SetFlag barbarian_knight:first_knight
  * The Barbarian. The Knight covers the flank. -> barbarian_first
    do: AddCohesion barbarian knight 6
    do: AddTrust knight -3
    do: SetFlag barbarian_knight:first_barbarian
  * Side by side. Shield and axe on the same step. -> side
    do: AddCohesion barbarian knight 10
    do: SetFlag barbarian_knight:first_side
  * The oath was to the hold, not the hall. The Barbarian's part of the hold now. -> hold
    if: FlagSet knight:oath_people
    do: AddCohesion barbarian knight 10
    do: AddTrust knight 2
    do: SetFlag barbarian_knight:first_hold

node knight_first barbarian
  Second. Fine. But if I see the shield go down, I'm not waiting for permission.
  -> captain

node barbarian_first knight
  The flank. Fine. It's a good flank. I'll keep it, and I'll keep my opinions about it, too.
  -> captain

node side knight
  Same step. That's not in any drill I ever learned. We'll practise it. You'll keep time badly.
  -> captain

node hold knight
  Part of the hold. The well children would have run from you. Then they'd have followed you everywhere. All right. Before the hold means before you too.
  -> captain

node captain barbarian
  Your Captain sold your hold to the beam. My collector laughed at the well. If we ever get there and that Captain's in the hall, what then?
  * We go to the Knight's sister first. Both of you at her door. -> sister
    if: FlagSet knight:sister_promised
    do: AddCohesion barbarian knight 10
    do: SetFlag barbarian_knight:captain_sister
  * Neither of you swings at the Captain without my word. -> word
    do: AddCohesion barbarian knight 4
    do: AddTrust barbarian -2
    do: SetFlag barbarian_knight:captain_word
  * Then the Captain sees both of you coming, and does the sum. -> both
    do: AddCohesion barbarian knight 8
    do: SetFlag barbarian_knight:captain_both
  * Stand beside the ones who stand. You cut it yourself. That's the Barbarian. -> beside
    if: FlagSet knight:line_beside
    do: AddCohesion barbarian knight 10
    do: AddTrust knight 3
    do: SetFlag barbarian_knight:captain_beside

node sister knight
  My sister will take one look at you and hand you a bucket. That's how she says welcome. Carry it up from the well, and she'll never forget your name.
  -> close

node word barbarian
  Your word. Aye. Say it quick when the time comes, Commander. I'll be counting.
  -> close

node both knight
  Both of us. Shield in front, axe a step behind and to the left. The Captain never could count past two.
  -> close

node beside knight
  Beside. I did cut that. I didn't know I meant you. Hand me the whetstone, Barbarian. I'm not taking your mark out. I'm smoothing it, so it stays.
  -> close

node close commander
  The Knight works the whetstone round the axe-bite. The Barbarian holds the shield steady on both knees, and neither of them suggests changing places.
